  "source": {
    "title": "Londonderry Standard, 18 January 1929, p. 7 (\"Coleraine municipal elections: chairman heads the poll\")",
    "publisher": "Londonderry Standard (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "sixteen elected and five defeated, all with printed votes; 21 candidates accounted for.",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0005986/19290118/115/0007"
  },
  "note": "First election of the new Coleraine Borough Council, polled Tuesday 15 January 1929; twenty-one candidates for sixteen seats (Londonderry Standard, 18 January 1929, p. 7). The report says 21 candidates for 16 seats: thirteen Ratepayers' Committee nominees, three British Legion, and five members of the old urban council standing independently. The four candidates topping the poll became aldermen. Party labels are those printed in brackets; the five independents carry none."
